17] [17592186243838 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243838 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243838 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186242934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243838 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e65bb2ef-90c6-598e-9157-9a8edd5838b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d4770f9-017d-5451-ade2-ef9bc61cba33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244122 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244122 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108325" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244122 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244122 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244122 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "23026cc4-61f1-51ff-9518-0d934ee1dfc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244122 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244124 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108337" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244124 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244124 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba20f45e-ea9a-5cbd-a036-8965c362108b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244124 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302595 #edb/ref 1080 "No intersection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302595 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302595 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "153f3c4f-9bb4-575a-bf5e