$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-4⟩+t⟨2,4,3⟩,\\,Π:4x+3y+4z-60=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304971 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c249fd8c-dcff-5201-89e1-bb6d2a206072" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304971 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,8,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312080 #edb/ref 1080 "(-20,31,13)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312080 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312080 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0eb8f532-8109-56ef-8ea6-7d7e8fda174e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312369 #edb/ref 1080 "(-20,13,31)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312369 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312369 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313291 #edb/ref 1080 "(-2,13,1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313291 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313291 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a7f8512a-48d0-5872-a500-e1de657bfe34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313762 #edb/ref 1080 "No intersection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313762 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313762 #edb/ref 10