}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399650 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399650 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186399654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399651 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3cd4a0b3-55ce-54d3-98c8-8b7021d46e30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399652 #edb/ref 1080 "(13,7,2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399652 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399652 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c181d54f-7b5e-5